   "verdict": "Petrie's cubit is 20.620 ± 0.005 in = 0.52375 ± 0.00013 m; π/6 = 0.52360 m sits 1.17 Petrie errors below it. Three literal digits agree. The metre was defined 4,300 years later from a survey of the Paris meridian, so the match cannot have been designed; and a 0.52 m cubit is simply forearm-sized.",
   "source": "Petrie 1883 s.136 (20.620 ± .005), s.52 (20.632 ± .004 in the King's Chamber)",
