   "literal_digits": 3,
   "rel_error": 0.0024897048932731036,
   "grade": "Confirmed",
   "verdict": "Petrie's casing angle is 53°10′ ± 4′; a 3-4-5 face is 53.1301° (53°07′48″), inside his error. The height a 3-4-5 needs is 5649.9 in against his 5,664 ± 13 in (1.08 errors). In Egyptian terms this is a seked of 5¼ palms, the slope the Rhind papyrus uses in its pyramid problems. Designed, most likely, but as a builder's ratio: no evidence they knew 3²+4²=5² as a theorem.",
