   "grade": "Likely (shape) / Suspected as design",
   "verdict": "Shape: the pyramids' spacing ratio is 1.072 against the belt's 0.979, and the bend is 11.5° against 7.2°. That is a fair likeness, 4 degrees apart in the bend. Against it: the brightest belt star is the middle one (Alnilam, 1.69 mag) while the biggest pyramid is the end one; to lay the belt on the plan you must put south at the top; and three points always make a bent row, so only two numbers (ratio and bend) are tested. Pin the two end stars on Khufu and Menkaure and the middle star lands 28 m from Khafre's centre (its base is 215 m wide); and the pinned map sits 36° away from south-up in 2560 BC, 13° in 10,500 BC. Bauval's wider map (Dahshur, Abu Roash as other Orion stars) is not tested here.",
